# AI Tool Kart — Server environment.
#
# Copy to `server/.env` and adjust. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the only
# tracked env file and must never contain a real secret.
#
# Every variable here is SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never prefix any of these with VITE_
# and never copy them into client/.env.local — that file is compiled into the
# public browser bundle.
#
# The server runs with no configuration at all: every variable below has a
# working development default.

# ─── Runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# development | production | test
NODE_ENV=development

# PORT and HOST are deliberately unprefixed: hosting platforms inject PORT.
PORT=3001
HOST=127.0.0.1

# ─── CORS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated origin allowlist for the browser client. The Vite dev server
# defaults to http://localhost:5173.
#
# Commenting this line out falls back to the localhost development defaults.
# Setting it to an empty value disables CORS entirely, which is correct when the
# API is served from the same origin as the site.
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# ─── Logging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# json = one structured object per line (production). pretty = human-readable.
SERVER_LOG_FORMAT=pretty
SERVER_LOG_LEVEL=info

# ─── LLM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which model answers POST /api/assistant/chat.
#
#   mock   the default. Deterministic and offline; builds plans only from the
#          retrieved candidates. Needs nothing below.
#   xai    Grok, via the xAI Responses API with strict structured outputs.
#          Needs LLM_API_KEY. There is no fallback: xai without a key refuses
#          to start.
LLM_PROVIDER=mock

# The xAI API key (console.x.ai). Required when LLM_PROVIDER=xai.
#
# Set it ONLY in server/.env, which is gitignored. NEVER prefix it with VITE_
# and never put it in client/.env.local: anything VITE_-prefixed is compiled
# into the public browser bundle, and a published key is a revoked key.
# LLM_API_KEY=

# The Grok model id. The assistant uses the `strong` class. Unset means the
# adapter default, grok-4.7 (xAI's recommended general-purpose model, with
# structured outputs). `fast` is unused by this server.
# LLM_MODEL_STRONG=grok-4.7
# LLM_MODEL_FAST=

# Per-call ceiling, in milliseconds. A timeout ends the turn with a 503; it is
# not retried.
LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# ─── Database (Phase 2A) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string. Read by the Prisma CLI (npm run db:*) and the
# db scripts. Not read by the running server yet — the catalogue and the
# submission store still use their JSON files until the Postgres adapters land.
#
# Local (Homebrew postgresql@17, trust auth on localhost, no password):
#   brew install postgresql@17 && brew services start postgresql@17
#   createdb -h localhost aitoolkart_dev && createdb -h localhost aitoolkart_test
#   npm run db:migrate && npm run db:check
#
# Every db script refuses a non-local host. To deliberately target one (e.g.
# the Railway database, from a one-off shell), set DATABASE_ALLOW_REMOTE_HOST
# to that exact hostname for that ONE command — never in this file.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://YOUR_MAC_USER@localhost:5432/aitoolkart_dev

# Database tests (tests/db.constraints.test.ts) run only when this is set to a
# LOCAL database; they truncate its tables. Migrate it first:
#   DATABASE_URL=<same url> npm run db:deploy
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://YOUR_MAC_USER@localhost:5432/aitoolkart_test

# ─── Accounts (Phase 2B) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Setting DATABASE_URL above also enables /api/auth, /api/me and /api/admin.
# Without it those routes answer 503 and everything else works as before.
#
# The first SUPER_ADMIN is made from a shell (register through the API first):
#   npm run auth:set-role -- --email you@example.com --role SUPER_ADMIN
#
# In production the session cookie is Secure and named __Host-atk_session, so
# the API must be reached over https on the SITE's origin (the Vercel /api
# rewrite), and CLIENT_ORIGIN must list that site origin: the CSRF origin
# check uses the same allowlist as CORS.

# ─── Trusted proxy (Phase 3) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret that lets a VERIFIED Vercel → Railway proxy tell this server
# the real client IP (http/clientIp.ts), so rate limits key on visitors rather
# than on Vercel's egress address. Only trusted when the request carries this
# exact secret in x-atk-proxy-secret; anything else falls back to req.ip.
# Leave unset until the Vercel side is verified on a preview deployment.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48   (server-side only, never VITE_)
# TRUSTED_PROXY_SECRET=
